From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usb: xhci-mtk: halt xHCI controller on shutdown

The MediaTek platform glue does not provide a shutdown callback, unlike
the generic xHCI platform driver.  This leaves the controller running
across a watchdog reboot, where it can continue DMA into memory that the
next kernel has already returned to the page allocator.

The MediaTek driver stores its wrapper structure rather than usb_hcd in
platform data, so it cannot use usb_hcd_platform_shutdown() directly.
Add an equivalent callback which retrieves the primary HCD and invokes
the xHCI core shutdown method before the platform restarts.

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
---
 drivers/usb/host/xhci-mtk.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-mtk.c b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-mtk.c
index d9b865546d52..bd01d9444111 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-mtk.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-mtk.c
@@ -740,6 +740,15 @@ static void xhci_mtk_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	pm_runtime_set_suspended(dev);
 }
 
+static void xhci_mtk_shutdown(struct platform_device *pdev)
+{
+	struct xhci_hcd_mtk *mtk = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
+	struct usb_hcd *hcd = mtk->hcd;
+
+	if (hcd->driver->shutdown)
+		hcd->driver->shutdown(hcd);
+}
+
 static int __maybe_unused xhci_mtk_suspend(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct xhci_hcd_mtk *mtk = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
@@ -841,6 +850,7 @@ MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, mtk_xhci_of_match);
 static struct platform_driver mtk_xhci_driver = {
 	.probe	= xhci_mtk_probe,
 	.remove = xhci_mtk_remove,
+	.shutdown = xhci_mtk_shutdown,
 	.driver	= {
 		.name = "xhci-mtk",
 		.pm = DEV_PM_OPS,
-- 
2.47.3
